# XiaoWan Agent

XiaoWan Agent is a lightweight local web AI assistant powered by the DeepSeek API. It supports multi-model selection, session history, streaming responses, local automation controls, and optional Android ADB tools.

## Features
- DeepSeek model selector with multi-model support
- Session-based chat memory
- Streaming responses in the web UI
- Local automation command execution (opt-in)
- Android ADB device checking via tool endpoint
- Clean browser-based interface
- Environment variable support

## Quick Start

1. Create and activate a virtual environment

```bash
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
```

2. Install dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

3. Configure environment variables

```bash
export DEEPSEEK_API_KEY="your_api_key_here"
export DEEPSEEK_API_URL="https://api.deepseek.com/v1/chat/completions"
export ENABLE_LOCAL_AUTOMATION="true"
```

4. Run the app

```bash
python app.py
```

5. Open the app in your browser

```text
http://127.0.0.1:5000
```

## Project Structure

```text
.
├── app.py
├── README.md
├── requirements.txt
├── data/
│   └── chat_history.json
├── templates/
│   └── index.html
└── .env.example
```

## Environment Variables

```bash
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
DEEPSEEK_API_URL=https://api.deepseek.com/v1/chat/completions
ENABLE_LOCAL_AUTOMATION=false
```

## Security Notes

- Local automation and ADB commands are disabled by default.
- Set `ENABLE_LOCAL_AUTOMATION=true` only if you explicitly want local command execution.
- Keep your API key in a secure environment or local secret store.

## Notes

This project is intentionally simple, local-first, and easy to extend. Potential next upgrades include:
- persistent database storage
- markdown rendering in the chat UI
- richer ADB device control and screenshots
- stronger session management and export/import
- deployment configuration for Docker or cloud hosting

